WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.564
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 1, Networking concepts, which is 23 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.564 --> 00:00:10.117
This lesson covers objective 1 point 8.

00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:14.110
Summarize evolving use cases for modern network environments.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.710
Today's concept: the two numbers to remember for VXLAN.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:24.844
Two virtual machines sit in different racks, with a routed IP network between them.

00:00:24.844 --> 00:00:28.150
They need to behave as if they share one Layer 2 network.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.750
So VXLAN takes the original Ethernet frame and wraps it.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:41.510
The wrapper is a UDP packet addressed to port four seven eight nine, plus a VXLAN header that carries the VNI, the virtual network identifier.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.539
A VLAN ID has twelve bits, so about four thousand segments.

00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:53.190
The VNI has twenty four bits, which is more than sixteen million segments.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.873
If an answer offers five oh six oh, that is the SIP voice port.

00:00:57.873 --> 00:01:00.010
VXLAN is four seven eight nine.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:07.756
For the exam, VXLAN means UDP port four seven eight nine and a twenty four bit VNI.

00:01:07.756 --> 00:01:12.688
Five oh six oh is the port for SIP voice, and a VLAN ID is only twelve bits.

00:01:12.688 --> 00:01:14.830
That's objective one point eight.
